1182
00:54:41.830 --> 00:54:42.830
(James) Mm?

1183
00:54:43.700 --> 00:54:45.080
Mm...

1184
00:54:45.200 --> 00:54:47.950
I’ll end it with this woman
and then I’ll do my fifth step.

1185
00:54:48.200 --> 00:54:50.200
That’s what I like to hear.
That’s good.

1186
00:54:51.700 --> 00:54:52.700
Mm?

1187
00:54:52.830 --> 00:54:53.830
Hey.

1188
00:54:55.450 --> 00:54:56.450
That’s good.

1189
00:55:06.330 --> 00:55:08.200
(Sombre electronic music)

1190
00:55:59.700 --> 00:56:01.080
(Music stops abruptly)

1191
00:56:04.200 --> 00:56:07.080
I don’t know the format here.
I don’t know the rules.

1192
00:56:07.330 --> 00:56:09.080
Did you not get the worksheets
I sent you?

1193
00:56:09.330 --> 00:56:11.830
- You sent me worksheets?
- Yeah. It's from this rehab place

1194
00:56:11.950 --> 00:56:13.200
- in California.
- I didn't--

1195
00:56:13.450 --> 00:56:16.950
It’s columns. Column one:
who you’re holding a resentment against.

1196
00:56:17.200 --> 00:56:18.950
- Column two: why you--
- I never got those.

1197
00:56:19.200 --> 00:56:21.700
- I’ve done it wrong?
- There's no right and wrong.

1198
00:56:21.950 --> 00:56:25.080
- I don’t want to do it if...
- There is no right and wrong.

1199
00:56:25.330 --> 00:56:28.080
- Yes, there is.
- There is no right and wrong.

1200
00:56:28.200 --> 00:56:29.830
- It’s the fifth step!
- So?

1201
00:56:30.080 --> 00:56:31.450
It’s all about right and wrong!

1202
00:56:31.580 --> 00:56:34.580
Things you’ve done wrong
and how you’re gonna make it right.

1203
00:56:36.450 --> 00:56:37.450
Let me see.

1204
00:56:44.080 --> 00:56:46.330
It’s, um... Haphazard.

1205
00:56:47.330 --> 00:56:49.200
- Haphazard?
- Yeah.

1206
00:56:49.330 --> 00:56:51.200
- Is haphazard OK?
- Yeah.

1207
00:56:52.200 --> 00:56:54.200
Course, yeah. I mean...

1208
00:56:54.450 --> 00:56:57.200
- Yeah. You don’t even need paper.
- I don’t need paper?

1209
00:56:57.450 --> 00:56:59.700
- Tell me what’s in your heart.
- If I don’t need paper,

1210
00:56:59.950 --> 00:57:01.580
why did I spend two weeks
writing this?

1211
00:57:01.830 --> 00:57:03.450
- Luka, just--
- This was hard for me.

1212
00:57:03.700 --> 00:57:05.330
- I don’t like writing.
- It’s good.

1213
00:57:05.580 --> 00:57:07.580
- You’re saying I didn’t have to.
- Breathe.

1214
00:57:07.700 --> 00:57:09.700
- I don’t want to breathe.
- Breathe with me.

1215
00:57:09.950 --> 00:57:11.330
- I don’t like breathing.
- OK.

1216
00:57:11.580 --> 00:57:12.700
(Audience laughs)

1217
00:57:12.950 --> 00:57:13.950
It's...

1218
00:57:18.830 --> 00:57:21.080
Just tell me
what’s on your mind. Hm?

1219
00:57:23.580 --> 00:57:26.080
Who, when you went through it all,

1220
00:57:26.330 --> 00:57:28.580
whose name came up most?

1221
00:57:30.450 --> 00:57:32.700
OK. Well, you.

1222
00:57:34.830 --> 00:57:36.080
- Me?
- Yeah.

1223
00:57:37.200 --> 00:57:38.830
- Not your dad?
- No.

1224
00:57:40.700 --> 00:57:42.200
What have you written about me?

1225
00:57:43.330 --> 00:57:44.450
I resent you.

1226
00:57:45.580 --> 00:57:46.580
Why?

1227
00:57:47.330 --> 00:57:49.200
- A few things.
- Like what?

1228
00:57:50.580 --> 00:57:52.700
You told me
I needed a spiritual awakening,

1229
00:57:52.830 --> 00:57:56.200
and when I had a spiritual awakening,
you tried to take it away from me.

1230
00:57:59.200 --> 00:58:00.450
OK. What else?

1231
00:58:01.580 --> 00:58:03.200
- You told me to end it with...
- Mm-hm.

1232
00:58:03.450 --> 00:58:04.450
- And I did.
- Yes.

1233
00:58:04.580 --> 00:58:06.080
And now I’m lonely again.

1234
00:58:07.200 --> 00:58:08.450
I’m sorry you’re lonely.

1235
00:58:10.330 --> 00:58:11.700
I miss my church.

1236
00:58:13.330 --> 00:58:16.200
- I see.
- I can’t go anymore cos...

1237
00:58:17.200 --> 00:58:20.080
- ...cos she’s there.
- And you feel I’m to blame for that?

1238
00:58:20.950 --> 00:58:22.200
- Yeah.
- Hm.

1239
00:58:25.830 --> 00:58:27.450
Who else is on your list?

1240
00:58:28.330 --> 00:58:29.330
No one. Just you.

1241
00:58:29.450 --> 00:58:31.580
(Audience laughs)

1242
00:58:34.080 --> 00:58:36.200
That’s your entire fifth step?

1243
00:58:36.450 --> 00:58:38.450
- A couple of resentments against me?
- Yeah.

1244
00:58:40.200 --> 00:58:42.200
- And this took you a fortnight?
- Yes.

1245
00:58:42.450 --> 00:58:44.580
You haven’t done it right,
you’ve done it wrong.

1246
00:58:45.330 --> 00:58:48.080
- You said there's no right and wrong.
- What you’ve done is wrong.

1247
00:58:48.200 --> 00:58:49.200
(Audience laughs)

1248
00:58:49.450 --> 00:58:53.080
- You literally just said it.
- It’s incomplete. You haven’t completed it.

1249
00:58:53.330 --> 00:58:54.700
- So it’s wrong.
- Incomplete.

1250
00:58:54.950 --> 00:58:57.200
- "Incomplete" is another word for wrong.
- Why don’t we take a moment?

1251
00:58:57.450 --> 00:58:59.580
You know what, James?

1252
00:58:59.830 --> 00:59:01.950
I don’t even believe
in AA anymore.

1253
00:59:02.200 --> 00:59:04.700
- Oh, OK.
- I’m sick of all the meetings.

1254
00:59:04.830 --> 00:59:07.450
- You have an illness.
- I’m not even sure it is an illness.

1255
00:59:07.700 --> 00:59:10.450
- Medics, scientists believe it’s an illness.
- No.

1256
00:59:10.580 --> 00:59:12.580
- Not all scientists.
- Most scientists.

1257
00:59:12.700 --> 00:59:16.330
Most professionals in the field
now accept alcoholism is an illness.

1258
00:59:16.450 --> 00:59:17.450
There’s a consensus.

1259
00:59:17.580 --> 00:59:20.950
You said yourself you inherited it
from your father. It’s genetic.

1260
00:59:21.080 --> 00:59:24.200
Everyone where I lived
was an alcoholic, right.

1261
00:59:24.330 --> 00:59:26.450
- Maybe it’s where you grew up.
- That’s a factor.

1262
00:59:26.700 --> 00:59:29.330
- But you have to go to meetings.
- What about Elton John?

1263
00:59:30.200 --> 00:59:31.080
(Audience laughs)

1264
00:59:31.330 --> 00:59:33.700
- What about Elton John?
- He’s an alcoholic.

1265
00:59:33.950 --> 00:59:36.080
- He doesn’t go to meetings.
- And look at him.

1266
00:59:36.200 --> 00:59:38.830
(Audience laughs)

1267
00:59:39.080 --> 00:59:43.080
- He’s still sober. And he seems happy.
- He doesn’t seem happy to me!

1268
00:59:44.580 --> 00:59:46.580
You can’t see
inside Elton John’s heart, James.

1269
00:59:46.830 --> 00:59:48.200
Maybe you're right.

1270
00:59:48.450 --> 00:59:51.580
Maybe you don’t need AA,
but you’re here now.

1271
00:59:51.830 --> 00:59:53.830
Why not just tell me
what's on your mind?

1272
00:59:53.950 --> 00:59:57.200
- Why not get it off your chest?
- I can get it off my chest to God.

1273
00:59:57.330 --> 00:59:58.950
- OK.
- I don’t need a middleman.

1274
00:59:59.200 --> 01:00:02.330
Well, how very Protestant
of you, Luka.

1275
01:00:02.580 --> 01:00:05.950
Well, how very Catholic of you, James,
to assume I need an intermediary.

1276
01:00:08.580 --> 01:00:09.700
I’m just offering to help.

1277
01:00:09.950 --> 01:00:12.450
- That’s all I’m doing.
- I don’t want your help.

1278
01:00:12.580 --> 01:00:15.450
I have Jesus now.
I don’t need AA.

1279
01:00:15.580 --> 01:00:16.580
And...

1280
01:00:17.080 --> 01:00:19.080
I don’t need you.

1281
01:00:22.580 --> 01:00:23.700
- The fifth step...
- Oh, fuck...

1282
01:00:23.950 --> 01:00:27.580
There is a confessional element to it,
a sacred element.

1283
01:00:28.580 --> 01:00:29.700
It’s confidential.

1284
01:00:30.450 --> 01:00:32.200
And I can...

1285
01:00:33.580 --> 01:00:34.950
I can forgive you.

1286
01:00:36.830 --> 01:00:39.200
- Forgive me?
- In a symbolic sense.

1287
01:00:39.830 --> 01:00:40.950
What are you saying?

1288
01:00:43.950 --> 01:00:48.450
I think the real reason
you’re not committing to this

1289
01:00:48.700 --> 01:00:51.080
is... you’re holding something back

1290
01:00:51.200 --> 01:00:54.080
because you’re worried
about my reaction.

1291
01:00:55.330 --> 01:00:56.700
But I want you to know...

1292
01:00:57.950 --> 01:01:00.950
...that you can tell me anything.

1293
01:01:06.950 --> 01:01:08.080
Yeah.

1294
01:01:11.700 --> 01:01:14.200
What if I told you something
and it made you mad?

1295
01:01:14.830 --> 01:01:16.580
- Mad?
- Yeah. What if you got mad?

1296
01:01:16.700 --> 01:01:17.700
I won’t get mad.

1297
01:01:21.950 --> 01:01:23.450
I heard something about you.

1298
01:01:24.830 --> 01:01:26.200
- About me?
- Yeah.

1299
01:01:26.700 --> 01:01:27.830
And I’m...

1300
01:01:27.950 --> 01:01:29.580
- I’m struggling with it.
- OK.

1301
01:01:30.830 --> 01:01:31.830
What was it?

1302
01:01:34.330 --> 01:01:36.830
There was a young woman
in the fellowship,

1303
01:01:37.700 --> 01:01:40.200
and someone told me
you thirteenth-stepped her.

1304
01:01:43.830 --> 01:01:45.200
- Right.
- Yeah.

1305
01:01:47.700 --> 01:01:49.450
OK. Right.

1306
01:01:49.700 --> 01:01:52.200
That's...
That’s a pretty serious accusation, Luka.

1307
01:01:52.450 --> 01:01:54.330
- Is it true?
- No.

1308
01:01:55.080 --> 01:01:57.700
- OK.
- Absolutely not!

1309
01:01:57.950 --> 01:01:59.450
- OK.
- I have never used

1310
01:01:59.700 --> 01:02:03.330
my position of authority
to sexually exploit a newcomer.

1311
01:02:03.580 --> 01:02:04.830
- OK.
- Who told you this?

1312
01:02:05.080 --> 01:02:08.200
- I can’t tell you who it was.
- I've never had sex without consent.

1313
01:02:08.450 --> 01:02:10.830
Let me make that abundantly clear.
Never.

1314
01:02:10.950 --> 01:02:12.700
- Well...
- Never, Luka!

1315
01:02:12.950 --> 01:02:13.950
- Yeah, but...
- What?

1316
01:02:14.080 --> 01:02:16.450
- Did you have sex with her?
- The person I’m accused...?

1317
01:02:16.580 --> 01:02:18.700
I don’t know
who you’re talking about.

1318
01:02:19.450 --> 01:02:22.450
Have you had sex with anyone
outside your marriage?

1319
01:02:23.200 --> 01:02:25.330
- Outside of my marriage?
- Yeah.

1320
01:02:27.450 --> 01:02:30.080
- Outside of my marriage?
- (Audience laughs)

1321
01:02:30.330 --> 01:02:31.330
Yes.

1322
01:02:35.200 --> 01:02:36.200
Outside...

1323
01:02:36.450 --> 01:02:37.700
(Audience laughs)

1324
01:02:39.200 --> 01:02:41.450
...of my marriage? Yes, I have.

1325
01:02:41.700 --> 01:02:44.950
But it was only that one time.

1326
01:02:45.080 --> 01:02:47.830
It was a mistake. I’m not proud of it.
But it was consensual.

1327
01:02:47.950 --> 01:02:50.700
But you made such a big deal

1328
01:02:50.830 --> 01:02:52.450
about me committing adultery,

1329
01:02:52.580 --> 01:02:54.580
saying it was wrong,
it wasn’t Christian.

1330
01:02:54.700 --> 01:02:57.200
- It is wrong.
- But you did it.

1331
01:02:57.330 --> 01:03:00.080
- And you pointed the finger at me.
- I’m not a Christian.

1332
01:03:00.200 --> 01:03:02.330
I was pointing out your hypocrisy.

1333
01:03:02.580 --> 01:03:04.700
Don’t you think I have a right
to point out your hypocrisy?

1334
01:03:04.950 --> 01:03:08.580
Yes, I suppose you do, yeah.
But it’s complicated.

1335
01:03:10.700 --> 01:03:12.330
- The woman that you...?
- Yeah?

1336
01:03:12.450 --> 01:03:14.950
- Did you make your amends to her?
- That's none of your business.

1337
01:03:15.200 --> 01:03:17.080
- You seem mad now.
- I’m not mad.

1338
01:03:17.330 --> 01:03:18.700
(Audience laughs)

1339
01:03:18.950 --> 01:03:20.330
What about your wife?

1340
01:03:22.200 --> 01:03:25.080
- What about my wife?
- Does she know about it?

1341
01:03:26.080 --> 01:03:27.950
- No.
- OK.

1342
01:03:29.200 --> 01:03:31.830
I never told her.
I should have. It’s hard.

1343
01:03:31.950 --> 01:03:33.450
What about your son?

1344
01:03:34.700 --> 01:03:36.830
- My son?
- Yeah. Did you tell him?

1345
01:03:39.080 --> 01:03:40.080
No.

1346
01:03:40.580 --> 01:03:43.200
- You said he was your best friend.
- He is my best friend.

1347
01:03:43.330 --> 01:03:46.200
- Why wouldn’t you tell him?
- We’re not close anymore.

1348
01:03:46.950 --> 01:03:49.950
- So he’s not your best friend?
- We don’t talk like we used to.

1349
01:03:50.080 --> 01:03:52.580
- Why not?
- I don’t know, you’d have to ask him.

1350
01:03:54.080 --> 01:03:55.580
Will you tell him?

1351
01:03:57.700 --> 01:03:58.950
I don’t know.

1352
01:04:01.080 --> 01:04:03.450
- If I’m being honest, probably not.
- Why?

1353
01:04:05.580 --> 01:04:07.330
- It would be hard to tell him.
- Why?

1354
01:04:08.330 --> 01:04:10.700
Well, for a start,
he doesn’t know I’m in AA.

1355
01:04:12.450 --> 01:04:13.950
How could he not know that?

1356
01:04:14.200 --> 01:04:15.830
- It’s personal.
- But he’s your son.

1357
01:04:15.950 --> 01:04:18.580
OK. Look, I didn’t want him growing up
with the belief

1358
01:04:18.830 --> 01:04:21.450
that he would inherit my... disease.

1359
01:04:21.700 --> 01:04:25.080
Cos it then... becomes
a self-fulfilling prophecy.

1360
01:04:28.450 --> 01:04:30.080
Did you tell your sponsor?

1361
01:04:31.830 --> 01:04:33.830
- What?
- Your sponsor. Did you tell him?

1362
01:04:33.950 --> 01:04:35.330
I don’t have a sponsor.

1363
01:04:36.700 --> 01:04:38.330
You don’t have a sponsor?

1364
01:04:38.580 --> 01:04:41.700
I’m 25 years sober, I don’t need someone
to hold my fucking hand.

1365
01:04:45.580 --> 01:04:47.830
- The woman that you...?
- Yes?

1366
01:04:48.080 --> 01:04:50.450
- Do you know who I’m talking about?
- You tell me.

1367
01:04:50.700 --> 01:04:51.950
They call her Mental Maggie.

1368
01:04:52.950 --> 01:04:55.580
- Mental Maggie?
- That's what they call her.

1369
01:04:55.700 --> 01:04:58.080
- You know who I mean?
- I mean, this is...

1370
01:04:59.450 --> 01:05:01.700
The woman was called Maggie, yes.

1371
01:05:01.950 --> 01:05:03.950
She goes to the Monday night
women’s group.

1372
01:05:04.200 --> 01:05:07.080
- I don’t go to the women’s groups.
- You were her sponsor.

1373
01:05:08.200 --> 01:05:11.080
- James, You were her sponsor.
- Yes.

1374
01:05:11.330 --> 01:05:14.200
You said people of the opposite sex
shouldn’t sponsor each other.

1375
01:05:14.330 --> 01:05:16.700
- But you did it.
- That’s how I know it’s a bad idea!

1376
01:05:16.950 --> 01:05:18.080
From experience!

1377
01:05:18.580 --> 01:05:21.200
- So you did thirteenth-step her.
- Uh-uh. No, no.

1378
01:05:21.330 --> 01:05:22.830
- But you had sex with her?
- Yes.

1379
01:05:23.080 --> 01:05:24.450
- And you were her sponsor?
- Yes.

1380
01:05:24.700 --> 01:05:28.080
- So that's thirteenth-stepping.
- I think it was more nuanced than that.

1381
01:05:28.200 --> 01:05:30.950
- How?
- I didn’t intend to have sex with her.

1382
01:05:31.080 --> 01:05:33.200
It wasn’t planned.
I was trying to help her.

1383
01:05:33.330 --> 01:05:36.830
She was a very troubled young woman
from the same kind of background as me.

1384
01:05:37.080 --> 01:05:39.450
I was trying to help her.
I was naive, OK?

1385
01:05:40.080 --> 01:05:43.450
One night, she propositioned me.
And I found it impossible to say no.

1386
01:05:43.700 --> 01:05:45.200
- OK.
- OK? That’s all it was.

1387
01:05:45.450 --> 01:05:47.950
- A stupid mistake.
- I understand that, it’s just...

1388
01:05:48.200 --> 01:05:49.330
- What?
- She’s mental.

1389
01:05:49.580 --> 01:05:51.700
She was not mental!

1390
01:05:51.950 --> 01:05:54.830
She's got mental health issues.

1391
01:05:55.080 --> 01:05:56.450
She’s got an eating disorder.

1392
01:05:57.200 --> 01:05:59.450
She always talks about
how she was abused as a kid.

1393
01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:01.700
Whoa! Whoa! No, I didn't know that.

1394
01:06:02.580 --> 01:06:04.330
- You didn’t?
- She never talked about that.

1395
01:06:04.450 --> 01:06:07.580
- But you were her sponsor.
- If she mentioned it, I don’t remember.

1396
01:06:07.700 --> 01:06:11.080
- I think you’d remember something like that.
- It wasn’t like today.

1397
01:06:11.330 --> 01:06:13.330
- What do you mean?
- Attitudes towards sex!

1398
01:06:13.580 --> 01:06:16.450
- It was different then!
- Different then? It was five years ago.

1399
01:06:16.580 --> 01:06:17.830
Who told you this?

1400
01:06:18.080 --> 01:06:21.080
- I can’t reveal my sources.
- "I can’t reveal my fucking sources."

1401
01:06:21.330 --> 01:06:23.200
Was it five years ago?

1402
01:06:24.080 --> 01:06:26.950
- Yeah, it was about that.
- How was it different then?

1403
01:06:27.830 --> 01:06:30.830
I mean, in a generational sense.

1404
01:06:31.080 --> 01:06:34.330
Your generation is too judgemental.

1405
01:06:34.450 --> 01:06:36.580
About sex. About everything.

1406
01:06:36.700 --> 01:06:38.580
Men of my generation,

1407
01:06:38.830 --> 01:06:41.950
we have a different idea
of what constitutes consent.

1408
01:06:42.200 --> 01:06:44.200
(Audience reacts)

1409
01:06:44.450 --> 01:06:48.080
- What? So it wasn’t consensual?
- No! It was! It was consensual!

1410
01:06:48.330 --> 01:06:51.450
OK? I grew up with a different idea
about sex than you did.

1411
01:06:51.580 --> 01:06:53.200
You never thought
about mental health

1412
01:06:53.450 --> 01:06:55.580
or what the woman’s age was.

1413
01:06:55.830 --> 01:06:59.080
As long as she was over 18, it was fine.
You took your chances where you got 'em.

1414
